  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Orbitals of&nbsp;equal energy are called degenerated orbitals. Homonuclear molecules are the molecules composed of only one type of element and contain following set of degenerated orbitals:</p><p>As, energy of,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub></math></p><p>Thus, only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></msub></math> are degenerate orbitals.</p></blockquote>",
